.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt SIDECAR 5
.Os ELSEWHERE
.Sh NAME
.Nm sidecar
.Nd description of an exact byte range, schema weft-byte-range/1
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A sidecar describes one range of bytes in some content that is identified
by its SHA256.
It is a separate UTF-8 Markdown file in two parts: a restricted header that
programs act on, and a Markdown body that people read.
The body may describe context, authorship, associations and purpose.
Neither part grants authority or executes anything.
.Pp
The sidecar's own bytes have their own identity.
Editing the description does not change the address of the bytes it
describes, and moving or renaming either file changes neither identity.
.Ss Identity and range
The content is identified by the SHA256 of its complete, exact bytes,
including any final newline, together with its complete size in bytes.
The range is half-open:
.Ql [offset, offset + length) .
All three numbers are unsigned byte counts from 0 to 18446744073709551615.
A reader checks
.Ql offset <= content_size
and
.Ql length <= content_size - offset
before any addition, and refuses a range outside the content; it never
clamps it.
A zero-length range at the end of the content is valid.
An unknown span is never written as a zero-length range.
.Ss Header grammar
The file begins with the exact line
.Ql ---
and a newline.
Each entry is exactly
.Ql key: \(dqvalue\(dq
and a newline: the key, a colon, one space, and the value in double quotes.
Another exact
.Ql ---
line closes the header.
There is no byte order mark, directive, comment, blank line, indentation,
trailing white space, tab or carriage return in the header.
Values contain only their key's alphabet, so there are no escapes.
The header, including both delimiters, is at most 1024 bytes, and the whole
sidecar at most 1048576 bytes.
This grammar is a restricted subset of YAML 1.2, the one
.Xr jobcard 5
defines; a general YAML parser does not establish that a file follows it.
.Ss Keys
The first five keys are required exactly once.
.Cm docid
and
.Cm revision_sha256
are present together or not at all.
Readers accept any order; writers use this order.
.Bl -tag -width "revision_sha256"
.It Cm schema
Exactly
.Ql weft-byte-range/1 .
.It Cm content_sha256
The SHA256 of the complete content, as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits.
.It Cm content_size
The complete size of the content in bytes, as a canonical unsigned
decimal:
.Ql 0
or
.Ql [1-9][0-9]* ,
at most 18446744073709551615.
.It Cm offset
The first byte of the range, in the same decimal grammar.
.It Cm length
The number of bytes in the range, in the same decimal grammar.
.It Cm docid
Optional: the native document that holds this content, as 1 to 32 bytes of
.Ql [A-Za-z0-9._-] ,
not beginning with a dot.
.It Cm revision_sha256
Present exactly when
.Cm docid
is: the native revision, as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits, not all zero.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Cm docid
and
.Cm revision_sha256
the address is content-only and makes no claim about any document.
With them, a resolver must verify the revision record, its document, its
content digest and its size before it reports the binding resolved, and a
failure to verify them is never reported as content-only success.
.Ss Body
The body is everything after the closing delimiter, and may be empty.
It is data, never further header.
It is valid UTF-8 as RFC 3629 defines it: no overlong form, no surrogate
and nothing above U+10FFFF.
It holds no control character but tab and newline: no U+0000 to U+001F
otherwise, no U+007F and no U+0080 to U+009F.
Writers use newline line endings and end a body that is not empty with a
newline.
.Ss Refusal
A reader refuses a sidecar, and takes nothing from it, when:
.Bl -bullet
.It
the file does not begin with the exact opening line, has no closing
delimiter within 1024 bytes, or is over 1048576 bytes;
.It
a header line is not exactly
.Ql key: \(dqvalue\(dq ,
which refuses unquoted and single-quoted values, extra tokens, aliases,
anchors, tags, collections, nulls and multiline scalars;
.It
a key is unknown, which refuses merge keys, or duplicated, or a required
key is missing, or only one of
.Cm docid
and
.Cm revision_sha256
is present;
.It
.Cm schema
is any other value, including another version or another domain such as
text, image or audio coordinates;
.It
a value breaks its alphabet: an empty value, a sign, a leading zero, a
decimal point, an underscore, an exponent, a number over
18446744073709551615, uppercase or short hexadecimal, or a docid that is
too long, begins with a dot or holds another byte;
.It
the file holds a NUL byte, or the body is not valid UTF-8 or holds a
refused control character.
.El
.Pp
A resolver also refuses, with a distinct result, a range outside the
content, content over its capacity, content whose size or digest differs
from the description, and content it cannot read.
It never returns substitute bytes as the requested content.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The last two bytes,
.Ql bc ,
of the three-byte content
.Ql abc ,
with no newline:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
---
schema: "weft-byte-range/1"
content_sha256: "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad"
content_size: "3"
offset: "1"
length: "2"
---
# A small passage

The selected bytes are bc. This description is not the selected content.
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jobcard 5 ,
.Xr sidecar 1
.Sh STANDARDS
This page restates the
.Ql weft-byte-range/1
schema of
.Pa policy/ADDRESSING.md ,
edition
.Ql 2026-10-13.v3 ,
which governs where the two differ.
The body's control-character rule applies STANDARDS.md section 8.
.Sh CAVEATS
SHA256 identifies bytes; it is not authenticity, truth, authorization or
confidentiality.
A sidecar, a digest or a link never authorizes fetching, publishing or
crossing a private boundary.
.Pp
Extending the schema needs a new version with explicit reader and writer
compatibility, not new keys in this one.
